content:
I've updated the contribution, and the input is now 4 lines per turn instead of 72:
- one line per fighter: HP, stamina, current move, its frame, duck depth and a round kick flag;
- one line with the 38 body points, 8 values each (x y vx vy apart angle target strength);
- one line with two counters (turns since the last contact and since the last hit).

The stub now has 2 loops ("loop 2" and "loopline 38"), at most 8 variables per loop and 16 per turn (31 before), and the generated Java stub is 45 lines.

The rules did not change, and the input is still the whole state: a turn can still be simulated exactly from it.
